These have no header in Tile Packs, so they carry the copyright notice and
license from Tile Packs' LICENSE, which follows them:

  src/main/java/com/constsdestination/tilepacks/TilePackMigrations.java
  src/test/java/com/constsdestination/tilepacks/TilePacksTest.java
  src/test/java/com/constsdestination/tilepacks/PointManagerTest.java
  src/test/java/com/constsdestination/tilepacks/TilePackManagerTest.java
  src/test/java/com/constsdestination/tilepacks/TilePackMigrationsTest.java

  src/main/java/com/constsdestination/ConstsDestinationConfig.java: only its
    Tile packs section, which holds Tile Packs' settings, from its
    TilePacksConfig.java.

  src/main/resources/com/constsdestination/tilepacks/tilePacks.jsonc: Tile
    Packs' built-in packs, gathered by TrevorMDev with packs and fixes from
    Tile Packs' contributors (David Lord, Matthew Johnson, Blackberry0Pie, Vic
    Segers) and community. Each pack's link is where its tiles came from, most
    often the video that shows them. consts-Destination has no list of
    built-in packs to pick from: it reads this only to make the built-in packs
    you had on into packs of your own.

  src/main/resources/com/constsdestination/tilepacks/*.png: Tile Packs'
    icons. Tile Packs credits them to their makers on flaticon.com
    (https://www.flaticon.com/), as its code comments name them:

      add_icon.png            "plus" by Pixel perfect
                              https://www.flaticon.com/free-icon/plus_1828819
      copy_icon.png           by Pixel perfect
      delete_icon.png         "close" by Pixel perfect
                              https://www.flaticon.com/free-icon/close_1828665
      remove_icon.png         "minus" by Utari Nuraeni
                              https://www.flaticon.com/free-icon/minus_11433623

    Pixel perfect: https://www.flaticon.com/authors/pixel-perfect
    Utari Nuraeni: https://www.flaticon.com/authors/utari-nuraeni

    Tile Packs' README credits its icons as: "Icons made by Freepik, Utari
    Nuraeni, Andrean Prabowo, and uicon from flaticon.com", its Freepik link
    going to Pixel perfect's page; consts-Destination keeps the four above.
    The pencil on a pack's edit control is drawn in code by consts-Destination
    (EditCustomPackLabel.java).

